# The custom probes of the lab: the landing zone of the live example, in the format of the rules.
# preflight-plan.sh runs them on the clean entity with --probes, beside the catalog, so a run
# shows a custom probe on a real tenant. A company writes its own file the same way.
section: lab
title: The landing zone of the live example
about: |
  What the live example keeps constant: its regions, its cluster names, and the tag that its
  inventories find the resources by.
rules:
  - id: lab-region
    title: The cluster is in a region of the live example
    engines: [aws, eks, gcp, gke]
    tier: static
    severity: fail
    status: proposed
    what: |
      The live example runs in us-east-2 (AWS) and us-east1 (GCP). A cluster in another region has
      no cloud account of the example, and its inventory reads nothing.
    check:
      kind: static
      expr: |
        .entity.spec.cloudConfig.region as $r
        | if (["us-east-2", "us-east1"] | index($r)) != null then []
          else ["region \($r) is not one of the live example: us-east-2, us-east1"] end
    tests:
      - fault: fixtures/other-region.json
        clean: fixtures/clean-aws.json
  - id: lab-name
    title: The cluster name shares no prefix with the other cluster of the example
    engines: [all]
    tier: static
    severity: warn
    status: seen
    what: |
      The inventories and the listings of the example find a cluster by its name, and a name that
      is a prefix of another (`fred`, `fred-b`) matches both. The example names its clusters fred
      and barney for this reason.
    check:
      kind: static
      expr: |
        (.entity.metadata.name // "") as $n
        | if ($n | test("^(fred|barney|strata-preflight-[a-z]+)$")) then []
          else ["cluster name \($n) is not a name of the live example (fred, barney, strata-preflight-<engine>)"] end
    evidence:
      - kind: run
        ref: teardown lab
        note: a prefix search for fred found fred-b too
    tests:
      - fault: fixtures/other-name.json
        clean: fixtures/clean-aws.json
